{
  "capturedAtRevision": "fff7dc14",
  "compiler": "compileLayoutGeometry (legacy document adapter, retired by this slice)",
  "howCaptured": "A committed, throw-away vitest file (zz-legacy-observation.test.ts, deleted before this slice closed) imported the eight g1 legacy documents from __fixtures__/layout-g1-fixtures.ts plus the mesh rhombus/notch helpers and built the three scale-tier legacy documents, ran the retired compileLayoutGeometry once per case and wrote the reduced records below. Nothing is hand-typed; re-running the same file at fff7dc14 reproduces the bytes.",
  "caseAliases": "The g2 fixtures delegate to the g1 factories (layout-g2-fixtures.ts), so the g2 suite's documents are exactly these g1 cases: g2LineRectangleDocument -> g1-line-rectangle, g2LShapedDocument -> g1-l-shaped, g2AutoBezierDocument -> g1-auto-bezier, g2MultipleOpeningsDocument -> g1-multiple-openings, g2ProfileMatrixDocument -> g1-profile-matrix, g2ObjectMatrixDocument -> g1-object-matrix, g2InvalidGeometryDocument -> g1-invalid-geometry. The g2 render-order claims are observed through them.",
  "retiredCases": "g1-multi-floor, g1-multi-floor-bad-room and g1-empty were captured for completeness but are not converted: format 6 has one floor datum, so a multi-floor legacy document has no wall-first expression and the empty document is the wall-first empty document (asserted directly).",
